The issue is that `proc.standardOutput` returns a `QByteArray`, not a string. `editor.insertText` expects a string, and passing a raw byte array likely causes it to fail or output incorrectly to the log. Additionally, `alert()` expects a string, which explains the empty popup.

To fix this, convert the byte array to a string using `.toString()` or `readAll()` combined with decoding.

Here is the corrected macro code:

```javascript
var proc = system("/home/stefan/ARCHIVE/SCRIPTS/latex_automation/main.py");
proc.waitForFinished();
// Read output as a string
var output = proc.readAllStandardOutput();

app.focusEditor();
if (editor) {
    editor.insertText(output);
} else {
    QMessageBox.information(null, "Error", "No active .tex document found.");
}
alert(output);
```
